<h2><strong>Groundhog Day Background</strong></h2>
<p>Punxsutawney held its first Groundhog Day in the United States in the 1800s. The first official observance to Gobbler\'s Knob was made on February 2, 1887. It is said that Punxsutawney Phil (the groundhog) was named after King Phillip. He was called Br\'er Groundhog prior to being known as Phil.</p>
